        </profile>
        <profile name="The Pythian Scales" id="ed17-2068-6482-d61e" hidden="false" page="95" publicationId="ca571888--pubN113187" typeId="57617267656172204974656d23232344415441232323" typeName="Wargear Item">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4465736372697074696f6e23232344415441232323">Provides 2 armour and 4+ Invulnerable save and immunity to Poison and Fleshbane rules.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Sire of the Alpha Legion" id="874b-8e56-b656-9796" hidden="false" page="95" publicationId="ca571888--pubN113187">
          <description>Alpharius has Preferred Enemy (Everything), Counter-attack, Move Through Cover, Scout, and Crusader which only apply once his presence has been revealed. Additionally, all models with Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) gain Preferred Enemy (Everything) when he is on the table and revealed.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="One of Many" id="4982-0611-fa4e-7df4" hidden="false" page="95" publicationId="ca571888--pubN113187">
          <description>Rather than deployming normally, Alpharius may deploy via the method described on p95 of HH:LAICL</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Insidious Mastermind" id="bf0a-de87-1e3f-cf87" hidden="false" page="95" publicationId="ca571888--pubN113187">
          <description>- May seize the initiative on a 4
- Units arriving via Outflank gain an extra D3&quot; to their movement on the turn they arrive
- From the second game turn onward, should the enemy player roll to successfully bring on a unit via reserve, and Alpharius&apos; army has a unit with the exact same entry type in reserve, Alpharius may roll a D6.  On a 4 the Alpha Legion unit immediately enters play this turn instead of the enemy unit.  Alpha Legion units which enter in this manner may still Outflank any may be targeted by enemy Interceptor fire.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
