        <selectionEntry name="The Dust of Devourers" id="16f2-7738-abca-560e" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="ddc7-d875-eecb-f69f" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
            <constraint id="8aab-9295-ebac-8f10" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0"/>
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Concussive" id="71bf-3b1b-00d5-cbb4" hidden="false" targetId="9d85-46f7-f5e6-a5f7" type="rule"/>
            <infoLink name="Poisoned" id="005f-f5f7-47cb-6fc3" hidden="false" targetId="a5ff-1cb1-bee4-d809" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <rules>
            <rule name="The Dust of Devourers" id="e322-70c4-23bb-e4ba" hidden="false">
              <description>Once per game in the Assault phase, instead of attacking normally, Amon&apos;s controlling player can opt instead to unleash the power of the Dust of the Devourers. This attack is struck at Amon&apos;s normal Initiative and inflicts D6 automatic hits on the unit Amon is fighting if it comprises five models or less, and 2D6 automatic hits if the unit comprises six models or more. These hits have no Strength, but have the Poisoned (4) and Concussive special rules and an AP of 4.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntry>
