        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Bitter Blood" id="a57d-90ff-4f5b-3f10" hidden="false" page="246" publicationId="ca571888--pubN89821">
          <description>Endryd Haar and any unit he has joined may re-roll failed To Wound rolls in the first round of an assault with any unit from the Traitor faction.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Warlord: The Fangs of the Emperor" id="0a9f-4dab-bd16-d7bd" hidden="false">
          <description>While Endryd Haar is in play, pick up to three power armour-equipped infantry units with the Legiones Astartes special rule and which do not have Dedicated Transports. These units gain the Scout special rule and cannot be Pinned (and cannot Go To Ground) during the game.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Savage Disipline" id="78fe-a89b-311d-5ef1" hidden="false">
          <description>Any unit with the Legiones Astartes (World Eaters) special rule ignores the Bloodlust special rule if it has been joined by Endryd Haar.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Incarnate Violence" id="2bf1-05bd-2db0-0a13" hidden="false">
          <description>Endryd gains the Furious Charge special rule once he or a unit that contains his model has destroyed another unit in close combat or caused one to Fall Back after a victorious Assault phase. Endryd Haar gains I WS when fighting in a Challenge, and if he kills a Character model in a Challenge adds an additional I to his side&apos;s Combat Resolution score for that Assault phase.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
