      </modifiers>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="The Wildfire Panoply" id="ad7f-86da-37cb-c186" hidden="false" page="227" publicationId="ca571888--pubN103311" typeId="57617267656172204974656d23232344415441232323" typeName="Wargear Item">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4465736372697074696f6e23232344415441232323">The Wildfire Panoply provides a 2+ Armour save and a 5+ invulnerable save during the Shooting phase and a 3+ Invulnerable save during the Assault Phase, including when targeted by Overwatch attacks. In addition it grants the Khan the Move Through Cover special rule.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Sire of the White Scars" id="544d-4476-b1b6-61f9" hidden="false">
          <description>In the first turn of any combat, Jaghatai Khan always strikes first, before any other models, but after Hammer of Wrath. If any other model also automatically strikes first, then use the two modesl Initiative values to decide which of them will strike first shouild the two meet in combat. When Jaghatai Khan is included as part of an army, all friendly modesl the the Legiones Astares (White Scars) special rule that are also part of the arm gain the Scout special rule.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="The Bleak Wind" id="7390-0a40-9dfd-e0e1" hidden="false">
          <description>Jaghatai Khan and any unit with the Legiones Astares (White Scars) special rule that he joins gains the Hit and Run special rule.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Lightning from Blue Skies" id="807d-b0a5-2af3-6aad" hidden="false">
          <description>When held in reserve, do not roll for Jaghatai Khan or any unit he is considered to be part of while in reserve. Instead the controlling player should note down the turn on which Jaghatai Khan and any unit he has joined will aririve on the table before the battle begins (this may not be the first turn, but may be any other turn. He cannot elect to stay in reserve). Similarly, when the Khan arrives on the table by means of the Outflank special rule. do not reoll for the table edge that he arrives on. Instead, the controlling player should note down before the battle begins which table edge the Khan and any accompanying unit will arrive from.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="The White Tiger Dao" id="ed19-c7c7-1493-2321" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
