      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Incaedius Booster Pack" id="1f77-4506-a233-62af" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="eb99-47b1-6cb6-7c06" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
            <constraint id="477f-6279-d7b1-add3" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Incaedius Booster Pack" id="a07d-5c66-aef6-597a" hidden="false" page="209" publicationId="ca571888--pubN103311">
              <description>The Booster Pack may be used once per game in one of two ways; these options are mutually exclusive and the use of one means the other may not be used in that game.

1) Deep Strike: The controlling player may choose to use this special rule to set up the Dreadnought in reserve and bring it into play using the Deep Strike special rule. The Deadnought is considered to eject the booster pack via a system of explosive bolt after landing and it plays no further role in the Dreadnought&apos;s operation.

2) Shock Assault: The controlling player may opt to deploy the Dreadnoughts as normal, in this case the use of the booster pack may be declared at the start of any of the controlling player&apos;s Movement phases. Including the first, or during the controlling player&apos;s Assault phases (but not both). If activated during the Movement phase, the booster pack allows the Dreadnought to move up to 12&quot;, ignoring all other model and terrain freely. However, if the model begins or ends that Movement phase in difficult terrain, it must take a Dangerous Terrain test. If activated during the Assault phase, the booster pack allows the Dreadnought to roll 3D6 to determine its charge range, ignoring all other models and the terrain freely. However, if the model begins or ends that Charge sub-phase in difficult terrain, it must take a Dangerous Terrain test. In etierh case, the Dreadnought is considered to eject the booster pack via a system of explosive bolts at the end of whichever phase it was used and it plays no further role in the Dreadnought&apos;s operation.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Exchange Talons of Perdition" id="8dc1-b970-299a-c985" collective="false" defaultSelectionEntryId="4819-5c6c-0c02-6d91" hidden="false" import="true">
