          </infoLinks>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Volkite Carronade" id="d0cb-3bd8-df16-3847" hidden="false" page="71" publicationId="ca571888--pubN80998" typeId="576561706f6e23232344415441232323" typeName="Weapon">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Range" typeId="52616e676523232344415441232323">48&quot;</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="537472656e67746823232344415441232323">8</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="AP" typeId="4.1502323234441545e+23">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Type" typeId="5.479706523232345e+27">Primary Weapon 1, Ignores Cover, Heavy Beam, Deflagrate, Haywire</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Heavy Beam" id="39b7-3cb7-5a93-2d06" hidden="false" page="71" publicationId="ca571888--pubN80998">
              <description>Draw a line from the end of the barrel to the max range of the weapon 1&quot; wide.  The initial target (first model in the path) must be an enemy model.

- All models in the beam area are hit, except Zooming Flyers, swooping monstrous creatures, and flying gargantuan creatures.
- Units struck are hit as many times as models are under the beam.
- If the beam strikes a Super-heavy vehicle, Gargantuan creature, or large intact building/fortification (bastion or bigger) the line of effect will not go any further.  The blocking target suffers 1D3 hits instead of 1.
- If a vehicle transporting models suffers a penetrating hit, the occupants suffer D6 Str4 AP- hits with the Deflagrate special rule.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
