                <profile name="Cytheron pattern aegis" id="8290-4c8c-3178-b5b0" hidden="false" page="165" publicationId="690c-3e82-3080-6bc0" typeId="57617267656172204974656d23232344415441232323" typeName="Wargear Item">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4465736372697074696f6e23232344415441232323">The Cytheron pattern aegis can be used in one of two ways: it can either provide the bearer with a 4+ Invulnerable save against Shooting attacks and a 5+ Invulnerable save against Melee attack, or it can be deployed. The controllling player may choose to deploy the Cytheron pattern aegis at the end of any of their own Movement phases (the unite must be dpeloyed on the table and not embarked upon a Transport vehicle of any kind) as long as at least two models in the unit are equppted with Cytheron pattern aegis. While deployed, the enitre unit gains a 4+ Invulnerable save against Shooting attacks and a 5+ Invulnerable save against Melee attacks, and any models engaging the unit in an assault have their Initiative reduced by -1. However, while deployed, the models equipped with Cytheron pattern aegis may neither make Shooting or Melee attacks. The controller player may choose to end the deployment at the start o fany of their own Movement phases, or if the number of Cytheron pattern aegis-equipped models in the unit drops below tow, the effect immediately ends.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
