        <infoLink name="Counter-attack" id="7181-1cd3-fc23-a901" hidden="false" targetId="0900-71d5-1937-aa96" type="rule"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
          <conditions>
            <condition childId="a511-1645-ac77-af33" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Bearer&apos;s of the Blood Hand" id="eac3-c04b-5742-a931" hidden="false" publicationId="6490-b351-71df-886d">
          <description>A unit made up of models with this special rule must declare a charge if able when they begin the Assault phase within 12&quot; of an enemy unit. If there is more than one eligable target, the controlling player chooses the target of any charges made. Note that this does not allow models with this special rule to charge a different unit to one that they made a shooting attak against in the previous Shooting phase.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Ravaging Assault" id="ae85-b058-4f33-bd4d" hidden="false" publicationId="6490-b351-71df-886d">
          <description>On a turn in which they have charged, a unit with this special rule gains a bonus of +1 to the amount of wounds inflicted when determining who has won a combat. Additionally, they gain a bonus of +1 to the result of any Sweeping Advance they roll they make in a combat that they are on the winning side of. These bonuses do not stack with any other rules that incrase the amount of wounds inflicted when calculating who has won a combat and the result of a Sweeping Advance roll.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
